###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# All models were trained on a single Nvidia A100 GPU; the small model took
# about 6 days, the medium about 10 and the large 14 (kept as text in
# trainingHardware: the unit of mlips:trainingDuration is not fixed by the
# schema). Inference throughput is reported as figures (OpenMM, LAMMPS).

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Intermolecular force errors and relative errors of Table S1 are not encoded (no MetricProperty for them); only total energy and force MAE/RMSE are.
# - Property benchmarks (torsion scans, X23 sublimation enthalpies, liquid densities and heats of vaporisation, water structure, peptide free-energy surfaces, IR/Raman spectra) cannot be expressed as AccuracyMetric in schema 0.1.2.
# - The 'max L' of Table 2 is the equivariance order of the messages; it is kept as a paper-local hyperparameter and not mapped to mlips:numAngularBasis. The correlation order nu = 3 (4-body) is encoded as mlips:bodyOrder 3, following batatia2024mp0.
# - The two-phase loss weights and the learning-rate schedule are in the loss/algorithm labels; only the initial learning rate is a setting.
# - Radial basis size and readout widths are not stated. The MACE-OFF24(M) training-set size and its training time are not stated.
# - The MACE-OFF models are widely reused pretrained models; they are paper-local here (model-off23-S/M/L-kovacs2025, model-off24-M-kovacs2025) and become registry models when a second paper evaluates them.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
